Those settings go inside the SSH server configuration file:

```bash id="jlwm3e"
/etc/ssh/sshd_config
```

---

# Configure on Red Hat Enterprise Linux or Ubuntu

Open config:

```bash id="dh6q7w"
sudo vi /etc/ssh/sshd_config
```

or

```bash id="8fshkl"
sudo nano /etc/ssh/sshd_config
```

---

# Add These Lines Near Bottom

```ini id="7v8e1i"
Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com
MACs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com
KexAlgorithms curve25519-sha256
```

Example full section:

```ini id="f3s33h"
Port 2222

PermitRootLogin no
PasswordAuthentication no
PubkeyAuthentication yes

Ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com
MACs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com
KexAlgorithms curve25519-sha256
```

---

# Validate Before Restart (VERY IMPORTANT)

```bash id="7d72dl"
sudo sshd -t
```

If no output:

* configuration is valid

If error:

* fix before restart

