# Verify Active Algorithms

Check server-supported ciphers:

```bash id="xbhhc7"
ssh -Q cipher
```

Check active negotiation:

```bash id="fh2m7i"
ssh -vv user@server-ip
```

Look for:

```text id="2uk4jw"
kex:
cipher:
MAC:
```

---

# What These Settings Mean

| Setting         | Purpose                     |
| --------------- | --------------------------- |
| `Ciphers`       | Encryption algorithms       |
| `MACs`          | Packet integrity protection |
| `KexAlgorithms` | Secure key exchange         |

---

# Why These Are Recommended

| Algorithm           | Reason                                |
| ------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| `chacha20-poly1305` | Fast + secure, excellent on VPS/cloud |
| `aes256-gcm`        | Strong AES authenticated encryption   |
| `curve25519-sha256` | Modern secure key exchange            |

---

# Production Recommendation

Do NOT use old algorithms like:

```text id="h5ffcl"
cbc
md5
sha1
diffie-hellman-group1-sha1
```

Avoid weak compatibility modes unless supporting legacy systems.

---

# Check Current Effective SSH Config

Very useful command:

```bash id="t39mbo"
sudo sshd -T | grep -Ei 'ciphers|macs|kex'
```

Example output:

```text id="l22gq0"
ciphers chacha20-poly1305@openssh.com,aes256-gcm@openssh.com
macs hmac-sha2-512-etm@openssh.com
kexalgorithms curve25519-sha256
```

